      "id": "def-local-weak-solution-for-a-divergence-form-operator",
      "concern": "The Definition says its L²_loc-data notion is 'strictly weaker than the Dirichlet notion ... which asks for u∈H¹₀(Ω) and a datum in the dual of H¹₀'. As an unrestricted comparison this is inaccurate: H⁻¹ Dirichlet data need not be locally L², so a general Dirichlet solution need not meet this local definition's data hypothesis. For example, an interval Dirichlet solution with point-mass forcing has H⁻¹ forcing but no L²_loc forcing. The comparison should be restricted to the common L²_loc-data setting. The actual definition and its stated test-space equivalences are unaffected.",
      "severity": "presentation"
    }
  ],
