      "faithful": true,
      "note": "Opened cor-minimisers-are-classical-when-elliptic-regularity-applies. Its smooth case assumes a bounded C∞ domain, forcing smooth near the closure and a smooth boundary lift G. It subtracts G, proves zero trace and forcing f+ΔG, then applies the zero-boundary classical-solution corollary."
